# Ad-hoc run logs (findings are recorded in commits/run.json, not these)
/*.log

# Video-specific pipeline configs: source/model paths point into /datasets/
# and /runs/, both gitignored below, so these cannot run for anyone who
# pulls the repo without also supplying those files locally. Reference
# numbers/findings produced from them belong in readme.md/reports/, not in
# a config that only works on the machine that made it. offline_video.yaml
# stays tracked -- it is cli.py's DEFAULT_CONFIG and documents the default
# parameter choices, not one specific run.
/configs/pipeline/offline_video_0681.yaml
/configs/pipeline/offline_video_7938.yaml
/configs/pipeline/offline_video_stillness_heatmap_demo.yaml

# Same reasoning, plus: paired with the now-deprioritized anomaly-judgement
# calibration work (see readme.md "Anomaly detection: measured scope") --
# the goal is traffic-condition description now (reasoning.scope:
# traffic_window), not an incident record needing frozen, hash-locked
# per-event cases.
/configs/reasoning/accident*.yaml
/configs/reasoning/demo_*.yaml
/manifests/reasoning/accident*/
/manifests/reasoning/demo_*/
/configs/reasoning/wp1_demo_0681.yaml
/configs/reasoning/wp1_demo_7938.yaml
/manifests/reasoning/wp1_demo_0681/input_lock.json
/manifests/reasoning/wp1_demo_7938/input_lock.json

